      "description": "Watch Cardiff vs Swindon Town highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 9, 2026. The atmosphere at the stadium crackled with anticipation as two determined sides faced off in a high-stakes knockout fixture. On August 9, 2026, the crowd settled in for a gripping Carabao Cup clash that demanded everything from the players on the pitch. A First Half of Resilient Responses The encounter began with a shock as Swindon Town took an early lead through a Gabriel Osho own goal in the 9th minute. Cardiff City , however, showed immediate character. They clawed their way back when Yousef Salech coolly converted a penalty in the 29th minute. Just before the interval, the momentum shifted fully toward the hosts as Salech found the net again, heading into the break with a 2-1 advantage following an excellent delivery from Cian Ashford . Securing the Victory The second half proved equally chaotic. Swindon Town fought back to level the match at 2-2 in the 62nd minute, with Paul Glatzel capitalizing on a Joseph Hungbo cross. As both teams hunted for the winner, the breakthrough finally arrived in the 77th minute. Jack Moylan rifled a clinical right-footed shot into the top corner following a swift Cardiff City counter-attack. The closing stages saw Swindon push hard despite James Debayo being sent off for a second yellow card, but the home side stood firm to secure their place in the next round."
