      "description": "Watch York City LFC vs Swindon Town highlights and goals from League Two on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 12, 2026. Fans gathered in their thousands on September 12, 2026, to witness a high-stakes encounter as Manchester United took on Sabah FK . The atmosphere was electric, with both sides eager to make their mark in this early-season clash at Old Trafford . First Half Dominance Manchester United started the match with clear intent, dominating possession and pinning Sabah FK back into their own half. The breakthrough arrived in the 27th minute when Patrick Dorgu provided a clinical assist for Matheus Cunha , who slotted the ball home with his right foot. This opening goal set the tone for a dominant display by the Red Devils, who continued to threaten through a series of corners delivered by Bryan Mbeumo and Cunha . As the first half drew to a close, the hosts unleashed a devastating flurry of attacking football. In the 42nd minute, Bruno Fernandes doubled the lead with a composed right-footed finish following a key pass from Youri Tielemans . The onslaught didn't stop there; in the 45th minute, Benjamin Sesko connected with an assist from Bryan Mbeumo to fire home with his left foot, effectively putting the game out of reach before the halftime whistle even blew. Clinical Finish and Defensive Solidity Following the restart, Manchester United maintained their grip on the game despite a series of tactical substitutions. Mason Mount and Joshua Zirkzee were among those introduced to maintain the energy levels. The fourth goal arrived in the 68th minute, courtesy of Lisandro Martinez , who showcased his attacking instincts by finding the net with his right foot. The Red Devils' dominance was reflected in the 58% possession they maintained throughout the match. Sabah FK attempted to find a consolation goal in the closing stages and came agonizingly close in the 91st minute when Patrick Mbina ’s header rattled the crossbar. Despite this late scare, the United defense, led by Leny Yoro , remained resolute. The final whistle confirmed a deserved victory for the home side in front of a massive crowd of 73,685 , marking a fine display of tactical discipline and clinical finishing."
